Third-party content and provenance
===================================

This NOTICE records provenance and license for every vendored or bundled
component in riot, in line with the tractoverse package licensing rule
(verify that each redistributed library permits the exact use).

1. TinyXML-2 (bundled source, compiled into riot)
   ----------------------------------------------
   `src/tinyxml2.h` and `src/tinyxml2.cpp` are from TinyXML-2,
   https://github.com/leethomason/tinyxml2 (original code by Lee Thomason,
   www.grinninglizard.com).
   - License: zlib (permissive; permits use, modification, and redistribution
     with the notice retained).
   - Use: source files are bundled inside riot and compiled into the package
     shared object for the medInria FDS reader/writer.
   - Modifications: `tinyxml2.cpp` was modified to avoid `printf`/`stdout`
     per the *Writing R Extensions* manual ("R has its own input/output
     mechanism"). The original license header is retained in both files (as
     required by condition 3 of the zlib notice: "This notice may not be
     removed or altered from any source distribution").
   - Attribution: "TinyXML-2, original code by Lee Thomason
     (www.grinninglizard.com), zlib license." See LICENSE.md.
   - SPDX: Zlib.

2. VTK (linked, NOT bundled)
   --------------------------
   riot compiles against VTK headers and links VTK static libraries supplied
   by the 'rvtk' R package at install time (rvtk: https://github.com/astamm/rvtk,
   CRAN package rvtk). VTK source code is NOT redistributed with riot.
   - License: VTK is BSD-3-Clause ("VTK License").
   - Use: dynamic/static linking at build time only; no VTK source or binaries
     are shipped in the riot tarball. The installed package links the VTK
     libraries that rvtk provisions on the user's machine.
   - SPDX: BSD-3-Clause.

3. Branding (NOT bundled)
   -----------------------
   riot's website theme, logo emblem, and colors follow the shared tractoverse
